### Privacy Policy API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for privacy policy management endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, updating, and deleting privacy policies
### Note: This API may not be fully implemented yet. Check your routes configuration.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@policyId = your-policy-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp (if authentication is required)
### - @policyId: UUID of an existing privacy policy

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE PRIVACY POLICY
### ============================================
### Create a new privacy policy
### Language defaults to "en" if not specified
### Supported languages: en, ar, fr, es

POST {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Privacy Policy",
  "content": "This is the privacy policy content. It explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information...",
  "language": "en"
}

### Example: Create Privacy Policy in Arabic
POST {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "سياسة الخصوصية",
  "content": "هذا هو محتوى سياسة الخصوصية. يشرح كيفية جمع واستخدام وحماية معلوماتك الشخصية...",
  "language": "ar"
}

### Example: Create Privacy Policy in French
POST {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Politique de Confidentialité",
  "content": "Ceci est le contenu de la politique de confidentialité. Il explique comment nous collectons, utilisons et protégeons vos informations personnelles...",
  "language": "fr"
}

### Example: Create Privacy Policy in Spanish
POST {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Política de Privacidad",
  "content": "Este es el contenido de la política de privacidad. Explica cómo recopilamos, usamos y protegemos su información personal...",
  "language": "es"
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policy created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "policy-uuid",
###     "title": "Privacy Policy",
###     "content": "This is the privacy policy content...",
###     "language": "en",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 2. GET ALL PRIVACY POLICIES
### ============================================
### Get all privacy policies
### Returns policies ordered by creation date (newest first)
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)

GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policies fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "policy-uuid",
###       "title": "Privacy Policy",
###       "content": "This is the privacy policy content...",
###       "language": "en",
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### 3. GET PRIVACY POLICY BY ID
### ============================================
### Get a specific privacy policy by its ID
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)

GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policy fetched successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "policy-uuid",
###     "title": "Privacy Policy",
###     "content": "This is the privacy policy content...",
###     "language": "en",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 4. GET PRIVACY POLICY BY LANGUAGE
### ============================================
### Get the latest privacy policy for a specific language
### Returns the most recent policy for the specified language
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)
### Supported languages: en, ar, fr, es

### Get Latest English Privacy Policy
GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/language/en
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get Latest Arabic Privacy Policy
GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/language/ar
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get Latest French Privacy Policy
GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/language/fr
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get Latest Spanish Privacy Policy
GET {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/language/es
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policy fetched successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "policy-uuid",
###     "title": "Privacy Policy",
###     "content": "This is the privacy policy content...",
###     "language": "en",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 5. UPDATE PRIVACY POLICY
### ============================================
### Update an existing privacy policy
### Requires authentication
### At least one field must be provided for update

PUT {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Updated Privacy Policy",
  "content": "This is the updated privacy policy content..."
}

### Example: Update Only Title
PUT {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "New Privacy Policy Title"
}

### Example: Update Only Content
PUT {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "content": "This is the completely updated privacy policy content with new terms and conditions..."
}

### Example: Update Title, Content, and Language
PUT {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Updated Privacy Policy",
  "content": "Updated content...",
  "language": "en"
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policy updated successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "policy-uuid",
###     "title": "Updated Privacy Policy",
###     "content": "This is the updated privacy policy content...",
###     "language": "en",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T02:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 6. DELETE PRIVACY POLICY
### ============================================
### Delete a privacy policy by ID
### Requires authentication

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/privacy-policies/{{policyId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Privacy policy deleted successfully"
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Create, Update, and Delete endpoints typically require authentication
###    - Use: Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
###    
###    Public endpoints (no auth required):
###    - GET /api/privacy-policies (get all policies)
###    - GET /api/privacy-policies/:id (get policy by ID)
###    - GET /api/privacy-policies/language/:language (get latest by language)

### 2. LANGUAGE SUPPORT
###    - Supported languages: en (English), ar (Arabic), fr (French), es (Spanish)
###    - Default language: en
###    - Language is case-sensitive in the enum
###    - You can have multiple policies per language (latest is returned by language endpoint)

### 3. VALIDATION RULES
###    Create Privacy Policy:
###    - title: Required, string, max 200 characters
###    - content: Required, text (no length limit)
###    - language: Optional, enum (en, ar, fr, es), defaults to "en"
###    
###    Update Privacy Policy:
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - title: Optional, string, max 200 characters if provided
###    - content: Optional, text if provided
###    - language: Optional, enum (en, ar, fr, es) if provided

### 4. VERSIONING
###    - Multiple policies can exist for the same language
###    - Policies are ordered by creation date (newest first)
###    - GET /api/privacy-policies/language/:language returns the latest policy
###    - This allows for policy versioning and updates

### 5. ERROR RESPONSES
###    
###    Validation Error (400):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Validation error message",
###      "errors": [
###        {
###          "field": "title",
###          "message": "Title is required"
###        }
###      ]
###    }
###    
###    Unauthorized (401):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Unauthorized"
###    }
###    
###    Not Found (404):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Privacy policy not found"
###    }

### 6. SUCCESS RESPONSES
###    
###    Create Policy (201):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Privacy policy created successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Get Policies (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Privacy policies fetched successfully",
###       "data": [ ... ]
###     }
###    
###    Update Policy (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Privacy policy updated successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Delete Policy (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Privacy policy deleted successfully"
###     }

### 7. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Create separate policies for each supported language
###    - Keep policy content clear and comprehensive
###    - Update policies when terms change (creates new version)
###    - Use the language endpoint to get the latest policy for users
###    - Keep titles concise but descriptive
###    - Ensure content complies with legal requirements (GDPR, etc.)

### 8. COMMON USE CASES
###    
###    Case 1: Display privacy policy to user
###    1. Get user's preferred language
###    2. GET /api/privacy-policies/language/:language
###    3. Display the latest policy for that language
###    
###    Case 2: Update privacy policy
###    1. Create new policy version: POST /api/privacy-policies
###    2. New policy becomes the latest for that language
###    3. Old policies remain in database for history
###    
###    Case 3: Multi-language support
###    1. Create policies for each language
###    2. Users can switch languages and see appropriate policy
###    3. Each language has its own latest version
###    
###    Case 4: Policy history
###    1. GET /api/privacy-policies to see all policies
###    2. Filter by language if needed
###    3. View historical versions

